I looked at the code for HeartBeat and there are multiple bugs in the code. The first is in the TimerLoop which has code which looks like this:
```c#
    private void TimerLoop()
    {
        while (!_stopped)
        {
            Thread.Sleep(_interval);
            OnHeartbeat();
        }
    }
```
The two lines of code should be switched, call `OnHeartbeat()` first, then sleep. This way `_stopped` will be checked immediately before calling `OnHeartbeat()` instead of there being a 1 second delay between them.  

The next bug is in `OnHeartBeat()`. There's a catch block which logs if there's an exception thrown during any heartbeat checks:
```c#
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            _trace.LogError(0, ex, $"{nameof(Heartbeat)}.{nameof(OnHeartbeat)}");
        }
```
This should be wrapped with `if (!_stopped)`. If the service is stopped, then any objects provided from DI (which includes the ILogger instances inside of KestrelTrace) aren't valid to be used.
